// E0502: a braced import entry that names nothing the module offers - not a
// declaration, not a re-export, not a sub-module - is refused AT THE IMPORT.
// The entry used to bind nothing and say nothing, leaving a use site that may
// never exist to report it: a module deleted from the tree stayed imported by
// name in two files, and `import std::fmt::{ printn }` compiles clean if
// `printn` is never called.  Rust refuses both (E0432).  The diagnostic names
// what the module does offer, so the fix is in front of the writer.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0502)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::E0502ImportNamesNothingOffered;

import std::fmt::{ printn };
//~^ ERROR[E0502] `std::fmt` does not offer `printn`

function main() -> int { return 0; }
